request: Add a button that clears every movie whose `seen` flag is true from the watchlist.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist-store, watchlist  ("Seen" maps to the existing WatchItem.watched flag. Two units need to change: watchlist-store gains a clearWatched() method (bulk removal of watched items, order of unwatched items preserved, persisted like the existing mutations), and the watchlist page adds a "Clear watched" button that delegates to it, is disabled when nothing is watched, and updates the existing accessibility announcement. search, movie-detail and app only read store signals, so they need no changes.)
round 1: owners watchlist-store=ok watchlist=ok; oracle RED
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 1 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist-store  (tsc is green and every failure is in my own WatchlistStore acceptance tests: they called `new WatchlistStore()` outside an Angular injection context, so the pre-existing effect() in the store's constructor threw NG0203. The component acceptance tests, which exercise store.clearWatched() through the UI (filtering, disabled state, announcement), all passed, so the implementation looks correct. I am replacing the store acceptance test with one that constructs the store inside TestBed.runInInjectionContext and flushes effects before the persistence reload, then re-verifying. No behaviour change is requested; only watchlist-store is targeted since that is the only unit implicated by the errors.)
round 2: owners watchlist-store=ok; oracle GREEN
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 1 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 3: accept  (Oracle is green: tsc passes and all 41 tests pass, including the acceptance tests pinning WatchlistStore.clearWatched() (removes watched items, keeps order, no-op when none watched, persists) and the watchlist component's "Clear watched" button (removes watched movies, disabled when none watched, announces removal). The request is satisfied.)

